mind explaining what you mean and what is sdr&nbsp;

[/quote]

Could you clarify what you want me to explain further? There&#39;s a number of things there.

<br />SRD is &quot;System Reference Document&quot;. Sorry, that&#39;s super RPG geek terminology to just assume and type out-- it&#39;s definitely a bit deeper a geek dive than many have done in that realm. System means, broadly, &#39;how the game works&#39;, so an SRD is a &#39;document for the rules of the game&#39;. So the D&amp;D core book would be the SRD for D&amp;D, in a greater sense, but it usually means stripped down to the bare bones. No flavor text or anything-- just the rules and nothing but the rules.
